  These are the two typefaces the Elcano Flag design system ships, vendored
  rather than loaded from a CDN so the UI works on a host with no outbound
  internet access, and so no third party sees who is using it. Both licenses
  permit bundling and redistribution, including in a commercial product,
  provided the license text travels with the fonts and (for Nebula Sans) the
  Reserved Font Name is not used for modified versions. Neither is covered by
  the Business Source License applied to the rest of this repository; the OFL
  and the MIT/Bitstream Vera licenses govern them respectively.

  The files are the complete upstream builds (950 codepoints for Nebula Sans,
  1548 for Hack) — do not replace them with narrower subsets. A Latin-1-only
  subset silently drops Latin Extended-A, which is where accented sender and
  publisher names live, and the browser then substitutes a system font for
  those characters alone.

